exit: 0
--- stdout
aethyme update — explicit paired-binary updates (never runs in the background)

Usage:
  aethyme update check [--json] [--refresh]
  aethyme update plan [--channel stable|preview] [--version X.Y.Z] [--json] [--refresh]
  aethyme update execute --confirm <manifest-sha256> [--json] [<signature>]
  aethyme update apply [--channel stable|preview] [--version X.Y.Z] [--json] [<signature>]
  aethyme self-update ...    same as `aethyme update apply ...`

apply plans and executes in one step: it prints the plan, then installs it
with that plan's manifest digest. execute and apply verify the release
manifest's Sigstore signature whenever cosign is on PATH; <signature> is
--require-signature (fail without cosign) or --no-verify-signature. The
archive is checked against the manifest's SHA-256, both binaries must report
the release version, and the pair is switched together or not at all.

The release manifest is cached for 6h; --refresh bypasses the cache, and
AETHYME_UPDATE_CACHE_TTL_SECONDS=0 disables it. Only the answer is cached:
the plan is recomputed every run, so a reinstall shows up immediately.

Homebrew installs are updated with `brew upgrade aethyme`.
After either binary update, run `aethyme upgrade plan` in each enrolled repository.
--- stderr
